From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] installer: flush the ansible log before copying it

_ansible_run() writes the playbook output to the configured logfile and
copies that file into the target's /var/log, but never closes it. The
last buffer of output is still in memory when shutil.copy() runs, so
/var/log/ansible-stig.log on an installed STIG system ends mid-task,
without the PLAY RECAP, although the playbook finished successfully.

Close the logfile once the playbook has exited, before the return-code
check, so the copy is complete and a failed run leaves a full log too.
---
 photon_installer/installer.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/photon_installer/installer.py b/photon_installer/installer.py
index 0a3cd1f..9c388ae 100644
--- a/photon_installer/installer.py
+++ b/photon_installer/installer.py
@@ -917,6 +917,9 @@ class Installer(object):
                 else:
                     self.logger.info(line)
             process.wait()
+            if logf is not None:
+                # flush the tail (incl. PLAY RECAP) before copying or failing
+                logf.close()
             assert process.returncode == 0, f"ansible run for playbook {playbook} failed"
             if logf is not None:
                 shutil.copy(ans_cfg['logfile'], os.path.join(self.photon_root, "var/log"))
-- 
